  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) Surface tension is related to force and length as&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(IV)</p><p>(B) Pressure is related to&nbsp;force and area as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp; (III)</p><p>(C) Viscosity in terms of force, area and velocity gradient is given by&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(I)</p><p>(D) Impulse is related to force and time of application as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>dt</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(II).</p><p>So&nbsp;A-(IV), B-(III), C-(I), D-(II)</p>"
  }
